[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Start "sicilian-d6 5.Nc3"]
[Name "2...d6 and ...e6"]

5... e6 { Solid. The bishop on f8 can now come out, but the c8 bishop is shut in. [%csl Yc8] }
6. Nf3 Be7
7. Bd3 { With the c8 bishop shut in there is no pin to fear, so the bishop takes its best diagonal, aimed at h7. [%cal Gd3h7] }
7... O-O
8. O-O Nc6
9. Re1 { The rook stands behind the e-pawn. White has every piece out, and e5 is the push to look for. [%cal Ge1e5] } *
